      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 59-year-old woman with back pain underwent an F-NaF PET/CT bone scan. Unexpectedly, multiple foci of increased tracer uptake were present in the abdomen and pelvis, which corresponded to the calcified soft tissue masses. The subsequent F-FDG PET/CT not only confirmed increased FDG activity in these partially calcified mass but also revealed abnormal activity in noncalcified lesions. The pathological examination demonstrated that the patient had ovarian cancer."},
